{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>the place where the king's prisoners were bound</b> אסורי is ketiv and אסירי is qere — teaches that he was imprisoned ten years for speaking ill of ten brothers, and another two years for saying to the chief cupbearer 'if only you would remember me'" "<b>bound</b> Three times in the Masorah: two regarding Joseph, and one: 'YHWH releases the bound (ה' מתיר אסורים).' And this is what the Sages said: Potiphar's wife said to him, 'I imprison you like a dungeon.' He said to her: 'YHWH releases the bound (ה' מתיר אסורים).'"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:04.293236395Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}